%% An Investor may pre-order like a Customer (not the Batch's Operator or its members). Cancelling before paying (UC55) or letting the 15-minute QR
%% expire costs nothing. Connector A continues on part 2. Cancellation after the deposit (UC55): when the Batch does not open every deposit is refunded,
%% cancelled pre-orders included; when it opens, a pre-order cancelled after paying forfeits the deposit, which becomes Batch revenue (UC54). Connector B
%% continues the kept pre-order on part 3. Delivery starts once the boxes are harvested (part 5). A refused delivery or an unpaid balance forfeits the
%% deposit (Batch revenue ForfeitedDeposit) and ends this pre-order; its crabs go back to stock for the Batch's invoiced sale on part 5. Balance =
%% weighed kg × price per kg − deposit, where weighed kg counts the live crabs received; the transit loss is only recorded, not deducted again, and a
%% negative balance is refunded. Connector C continues on part 4. A return in the window (Customer, or approved by the Operator) or a complaint resolved
%% with a full refund returns the order; compensation, replacement or rejection keeps it Delivered until the return window ends (a partial refund also
%% creates a refund instruction, not drawn). An active complaint blocks completion. Each pre-order ends at its own flow final. This flow runs once per
%% Batch, separately from the flows of each pre-order (parts 1–4): the harvest per box, then, after the sales window closes, the invoiced sales
%% (low-grade crabs and crabs of forfeited pre-orders, reasons LowGrade and ForfeitResale) and one final order to the committed buyer, never below the
%% floor price. Traceability: UC25, UC27, UC55, UC12, UC40, UC22, UC29, UC30, UC54, UC33, UC31, UC32, UC50, UC51 (TP3 Nhân). Exception branches:
%% pre-order cancelled or unpaid before the deposit → nothing lost; Batch not opened → every deposit refunded, cancelled pre-orders included; cancelled
%% after paying and the Batch opened, delivery refused or balance unpaid → deposit forfeited (UC54), and in the last two cases the crabs are resold
%% through an invoiced sale; final-order price below the floor price → revised; return or complaint → refund, or the order completes after the return
%% window. «planned» in v1.4: farm map with delivery radius, pre-order by crab count from a minimum while the Batch is funding (the code pre-orders by kg
%% on a listing while InProduction), the forfeit rule on cancellation, the delivery note with the order QR, weighing at the door and the balance on
%% weighed kg, forfeited Customer deposits, invoiced sales of low-grade or resold crabs (InvoicedSale) and the final order at the floor price; every
%% delivered order has an invoice. Removed in v1.4 (still in code): product listings, retail cart and checkout, priority offtake claims, per-crab tags
%% and tag-scan packing, the balance before packing (PreorderBalanceJob). States: BulkPreOrder PendingPayment (crabs held) → DepositPaid → Confirmed
%% «planned» → Packed → Shipping → Delivered → Completed, or Cancelled, Returned, Refunded «planned», Forfeited «planned» (Figure 4.17); InvoicedSale |
%% FinalOrder recorded with its invoice (crabs Sold), PendingPayment → Completed when the OrderPayment is paid «planned» (4.18; cancellation or expiry is
%% an open point); complaint Open → OperatorResponded / Escalated → Resolved / Rejected (4.19). Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were
%% confirmed by the lead.
